{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5kiDS9rdj6wYhKyJKBj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, here are my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model at `Shipment.kt:9-14` with status field\n- ShipmentStatus enum at `Shipment.kt:23-27` with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED states\n- ShipmentRepository at `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-18` has `save()` and `ShipmentRepository.kt:22` has `findById()`\n- ShipmentController at `ShipmentController.kt:1-56` currently has create, getById, list endpoints\n- Exception handling at `ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` with ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum at `ApiError.kt:31-37` defines all error codes\n- GlobalExceptionHandler at `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-28` centralizes error response formatting\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (not manual response building)\n- ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409\n- Endpoints return ResponseEntity with appropriate status codes\n- All imports follow the same pattern (annotations, repositories, exceptions)\n- Tests use MockMvc with SpringBootTest annotation\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - add `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` - add new ErrorCode for cancellation rejection\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - add tests for confirm endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding a new ErrorCode must not break existing serialization\n- Idempotency: confirming already-CONFIRMED shipment must succeed with no changes\n- Must preserve all existing test expectations\n\n**Open questions:** None - the ticket is explicit about all cases.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_WHEN_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum. This gives us a machine-readable code for the 409 response when trying to confirm a cancelled shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new `confirm` method:\n   - Annotated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n   - Takes `shipmentId` as `@PathVariable`\n   - Retrieves shipment via repository, throwing `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throws `ConflictException` with the new error code\n   - If status is `CREATED`, updates to `CONFIRMED` and persists\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, does nothing (idempotent)\n   - Returns the shipment with 200 OK status (no explicit status needed for success)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add four new test cases:\n   - Confirm a CREATED shipment transitions it to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds with no changes (idempotency)\n   - Confirm a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with proper error code\n   - Confirm a non-existent shipment returns 404 with proper error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could have made the response status explicit with `ResponseEntity.ok(saved)` vs just returning the object, but returning just the object is consistent with existing `getById` endpoint which doesn't use ResponseEntity explicitly.\n- Could have used a different error code name like `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` but `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_WHEN_CANCELLED` is clearer about the operation that failed.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):*\n- Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n- Read: Repository retrieves shipment with status CREATED\n- Write: Repository saves updated shipment with status CONFIRMED\n- Response: 200 OK with updated Shipment object\n\n*Idempotent path (already CONFIRMED):*\n- Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n- Read: Repository retrieves shipment with status CONFIRMED\n- Write: No write needed (status stays CONFIRMED)\n- Response: 200 OK with unchanged Shipment object\n\n*Conflict path (CANCELLED):*\n- Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n- Read: Repository retrieves shipment with status CANCELLED\n- Write: No write\n- Exception: `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_WHEN_CANCELLED, message)`\n- Response: 409 Conflict with error envelope via GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n*Not found path:*\n- Request: `POST /shipments/missing/confirm`\n- Read: Repository returns null\n- Exception: `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)`\n- Response: 404 Not Found with error envelope via GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `confirms a created shipment to confirmed` - happy path, verify status changes from CREATED to CONFIRMED\n2. `confirms an already confirmed shipment succeeds and changes nothing` - idempotency test, verify status stays CONFIRMED\n3. `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` - error path, verify ConflictException is thrown with correct error code\n4. `reports confirming an unknown shipment with 404` - not found path, verify ResourceNotFoundException is thrown with correct error code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2372,"cache_read_input_tokens":17877,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2372},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"597f3a65-624b-4322-8502-0d05744a0915","uuid":"a0fe7667-d9b4-4899-94d2-7ea96854c568","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:11:16.199Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5kiCy7inuw1688tY3dZ"}
