{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5kmctd6cbVUvwYTir7n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass. The verification shows:\n- **Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n- **Result:** BUILD SUCCESS\n- **Tests run:** 17 total, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped\n- **ShipmentControllerTest:** 9 tests (5 original + 4 new)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** - BUILD SUCCESS shown in verification\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** - All 17 tests pass (original 5 shipment tests still passing)\n3. ✅ **POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm confirms a created shipment** - Test \"confirms a created shipment to confirmed\" verifies status changes from CREATED to CONFIRMED and persists\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent** - Using same ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) patterns as existing code, error code added to ErrorCode enum, GlobalExceptionHandler handles serialization\n5. ✅ **Repeated confirm succeeds, cancelled rejected, unknown rejected** - Three new tests cover these cases with proper status codes and error codes\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** - Only modified .kt files, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only modified ShipmentController, ApiError (enum addition), and test file\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Added one line: `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_WHEN_CANCELLED,` to the ErrorCode enum. This is necessary because the ticket requires a 409 response for CANCELLED shipments, and we need a machine-readable code.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added `confirm()` method (20 lines) implementing the four required behaviors:\n   - 404 if shipment doesn't exist (ResourceNotFoundException)\n   - 409 if shipment is CANCELLED (ConflictException)\n   - Transitions CREATED to CONFIRMED and persists\n   - Idempotent: already CONFIRMED return